  "provenance": "SYNTHETIC demonstration modelled on the published aluminium case described by Innoval Technology (Farley): 20-25 mm transverse bands whose pitch does not change with speed, 315 Hz at 470 m/min equal to 2 x BPFI of a work-roll bearing. Same synthetic stand and spans as the thin-gauge demo, BUT the work roll is 0.284 m diameter (radius 0.142 m): with a 0.40 m roll a BPFI order of 18.66 gives a 35 mm pitch and 221 Hz at 470 m/min, so the published numbers (BPFI ~18.66, 315 Hz, ~25 mm) are only mutually consistent with a ~0.28 m work roll. Bearing: 35 rollers, 16.47 mm, pitch diameter 0.24 m, 15 deg contact angle -> BPFI order 18.66. Pass 1.0 -> 0.70 mm, flow stress 230 MPa, friction 0.06, tensions 20/25 MPa at 7.8333 m/s. Pitch = pi*D_w*(1+f)/(2*BPFI) with the model forward slip; observed at 6.0 and 7.8333 m/s (same pitch), measured stand vibration 2*BPFI*f_wr at 470 m/min; no gauge variation, both faces, persists after work- and backup-roll change.",
  "notes": [
    "Closed-loop demo: the planted cause is an order-locked work-roll bearing defect (2 x BPFI)."
